    description: "RESIDUAL OF INV-midag, whose statement is general: every analyzer-origin calls edge with a line lies inside its src's span.\n\nINV-midag fixed and verified the analyzers its 26-repo measurement could see: kotlin, scala, swift, c, rust, ruby, csharp, haskell, javascript/typescript, and go. Go was clean on gin and logrus, but a fixture of `func init()` declared twice in one file showed the defect, so it was fixed too. java was verified clean with an overload fixture, and erlang/elixir by INV-mozas.\n\nThese analyzers also define an enclosing-function lookup, have NO repository in the measurement corpus, and have NO containment fixture. Their status is UNKNOWN, not clean:\n  lang-mainstream : groovy objc perl php powershell\n  lang-common     : dart elm fsharp glsl hlsl julia matlab nix r_lang scheme starlark wgsl\n  lang-extended1  : d_lang fennel fish gdscript gleam hack janet llvm_ir odin pascal solidity v_lang\n\nThe INV-midag gate (test_call_anchor_gate.py in each language package) lists every one of them as UNVERIFIED against this row. A new analyzer that defines an enclosing lookup and is not classified fails the gate.\n\nASKED, per language:\n1. Write a fixture with two same-named callables in one file, in the language's own natural shape: overloads, a redefinition, two classes, preprocessor alternatives, or multiple equations or clauses.\n2. Assert reach first, then containment.\n3. If it fails, key the lookup on position (core symbols_at / symbol_declared_by), after checking that the symbol span starts at the declaration node the walk reaches.\n4. Move the gate entry to VERIFIED."  # 99ff
    fields: {}  # 99ff
