  message: "DONE, PR #1184 (merged 2026-09-24; commits 5b728475da + bcca947e76).\n\nAll 29 analyzers now have a same-named-callables fixture that asserts reach first, then containment. All 29 are VERIFIED in the three gate files (test_call_anchor_gate.py, _common, _extended1). No WI-mapor entry remains.\n\n13 OF THE 29 HAD THE DEFECT: groovy, objc, perl, powershell, fsharp, glsl, hlsl, julia, nix, r, d, fish, gdscript. Each keyed the lookup on the declaration's NAME. Each now keys on its POSITION (core symbols_at / symbol_declared_by over file_symbols()). The other 16 passed unchanged: php, dart, elm, matlab, scheme, starlark, wgsl, fennel, gleam, hack, janet, llvm_ir, odin, pascal, solidity, v.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE:\n- MUTATION: the new tests, run against a pinned dev worktree, fail for exactly those 13 (plus the nix file-function test below) and pass on the fix.\n- CORRECTION TO THIS ROW'S PREMISE, \"no corpus repo\": whole_bunch_of_repos has them; they were only outside INV-midag's 26. Each analyzer was run alone on 18 repos, pinned dev vs fix, calls edges diffed as sets. Out of span, dev -> fix:\n    d dmd 15126/104963 -> 0\n    objc ResearchKit 1807 -> 0, ReactiveObjC 42 -> 0\n    glsl whisper.cpp 589 -> 0, gpac 3 -> 0\n    groovy clover 449 -> 0\n    perl postgresql 22 -> 0, git 17 -> 0\n    r spark 53 -> 0\n    0 -> 0 on jenkins, emscripten, podman, vscode, mlflow, crun, conmon, loki, postgrest\n  Every move is out->in. There is no in->in relabel and no in->out move.\n- No corpus repo for julia, fish, gdscript or f# (qemu's .fs is Forth). Those rest on their fixtures.\n\nONE BEHAVIOUR CHANGE BEYOND THE ANCHOR (nix): a call inside a file's own top-level function, but outside any function-valued binding, had a src only when a binding inside shared the file's name. The walk now recognises the file function. postgrest 13 -> 159 call edges, loki 2 -> 5, and every old edge is unchanged.\n\nALSO REMOVED: perl's _file_package_names, which had no reader once the lookup went positional.\n\nSIDE FINDINGS, filed separately: julia self-call from each definition's signature; scheme/fennel/janet drop calls inside nested definitions; pascal emits no symbol for a `procedure TA.Run` method; nix emits one edge per curried application level.\nInstruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mapor_09242026/."  # 72ef
